<https://github.com/corrado877/CognitiveBiasOntologies/tree/main/Confabulation%20Bias> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Confabulation bias refers to a cognitive bias characterized by the tendency to generate fabricated or inaccurate information to fill in memory gaps, often without the individual's awareness. In confabulation, individuals create false details or narratives to explain events, experiences, or gaps in their memory. This bias can occur as a result of memory errors, the brain's attempt to make sense of incomplete information, or a desire to maintain coherence in one's personal narrative. Confabulation bias can lead to the creation of vivid and plausible but entirely fictional memories, influencing one's perception of past events." .
_:N95e835d1f07541b59b313960438e55ee <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#unionOf> _:Nafaab4239b5544ada09d3a74d5b7e9b0 .
